Vi Quick Reference'' card,
An Introduction to Display Editing with Vi''.
.SH AUTHOR
William Joy
.br
Mark Horton added macros to \fIvisual\fR mode and is maintaining
version 3
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status 0 on a clean session; nonzero when the shared ex engine
recorded an editing or startup failure, even if the editor remained
usable.
.SH BUGS
At most 2048 lines, with bounded line lengths as described in
ex(1).
There is no gg, no full-screen replace mode R and no crash recovery.
There is no normal-mode filter command: ! (!!, !}) is ignored; use the
colon forms :%!cmd, :a,b!cmd and :r !cmd.
:w !cmd shows its output for a moment and then repaints, without the
hit-return pause POSIX requires after a command overwrites the screen;
:!cmd does pause.
A characterwise yank on one line holds 254 bytes.
This is an implemented subset, not all of Berkeley vi.
